| `Docs/Brand_Asset_Catalog` | Brand assets and brand asset rules. | Generic UI, WYSIWYG UI, official icon set. |

All catalogs use the same implementation-state vocabulary: `実装済み`, `策定済み`, and `対象外`.

Required Class Families in Generic, Admin, and WYSIWYG catalogs are a check-covered contract. Listed classes must stay present in the catalog and generated CSS together.

`Docs/Component_Contract_Matrix` maps component families to their catalog or specification owner, TypeScript source, generated output, JavaScript hooks, sample coverage, and check coverage.

## Layout Direction

Layout is meaningful rather than utility-first. Core layout, meaningful grid, Admin layout, responsive policy, and Layout Tokens are part of the system.

`Tokens/layout.css` owns structural values such as container width, sidebar width, layout gap, and gutter. Fine spacing remains in `Tokens/spacing.css`.

Layout System v2 adds named application structures: layout frame, header, footer, body, sticky/scroll regions, master-detail layout, workbench layout, dashboard grid, resource grid, and editor grid. These classes are semantic contracts, not low-level utility aliases.

Dialog, drawer, popover, toast, progress, skeleton, data table state, bulk feedback, stepper, and filter builder UI are interaction-ready component contracts. Their CSS, JavaScript hooks, catalog rows, and checks are updated together.

Interaction contracts include representative accessibility hooks: dialog roles, modal state, labelled headings, dismiss buttons, Escape handling, focus containment, hidden decorative content, current-step indication, and expanded/pressed state synchronization.

## WYSIWYG Editor Direction

WYSIWYG Editor UI is part of Adlaire-Design-System. Editor details are governed by `Docs/Editor_Master_Spec`; UI component coverage is governed by `Docs/WYSIWYG_Editor_UI_Catalog`.

The editor model is a safe structured content editing foundation with command, document, selection, history, validation, event, and type modules under `TypeScript/Editor/`.

WYSIWYG UI contracts include slash menu, suggestion card, save banner, lock banner, block reorder, comment, warning, readonly, disabled, locked, and accessibility panel states.

## Icons and Brand

`Icons/` contains the official 500 SVG icons. `Docs/Icon_Set_Catalog` governs icon categories, usage, semantic/decorative distinction, and alt-text policy.

`Brand/` contains brand assets. `Docs/Brand_Asset_Catalog` governs brand asset files, types, formats, and descriptions.

## Samples

Samples are confirmation aids. `Samples/design/index.html` covers Generic UI, Admin UI, WYSIWYG Editor UI, Git Provider UI, Tokens, Brand, and the official 500 SVG icons.

Samples must not become the source of truth for tokens, CSS contracts, JavaScript behavior, or catalog state.

Checks keep representative sample coverage for Layout System v2, operational feedback, and WYSIWYG state UI so sample drift is visible without making Samples authoritative.

## Checks

Normal check:

```sh
sh Tools/check/check-adlaire-design.sh
```

Release check:

```sh
sh Tools/check/check-adlaire-design.sh --release-check
```

The release check assumes `git fetch backup --prune`, local `main` synchronized with `backup/main`, matching merged branch cleanup, and no patches outside `backup/main`.

Checks verify required class families, forbidden dependency/build artifacts, direct UI color literals, accessibility hooks, required JavaScript hooks across source and generated files, token source/generated CSS consistency, token file inventory consistency, duplicate token definitions, UI source/generated CSS consistency, undefined CSS variable usage, incomplete WYSIWYG selectors, sample coverage, and post-merge release readiness.

Check failures use family-labelled diagnostics so the broken contract area is visible before reading the full failure details.

